2026-11-17 Cara integration: native Mac atlas/render-worker queue and owned uploads,
checked GPU remapping, shader source cache, conservative diagnostic suffix sharing,
source/host-span capture and attribution, developer game menu and CPU-only tests.
Derived emulator changes retain the existing Citra/MMJ GPL notices. Experimental
paths remain explicit opt-ins; these changes do not authorize omitted GPU work.

Optional ordered shader extra-word stream dispatch: batching concept referenced
from Azahar PR #2318, commit c688076ac96491bd0d390fc8e6d8325fd3fb420f,
authored by PabloMK7 and Wunkolo. Cara retains per-word operations and does not
import deferred renderer dirtiness or unchanged-word suppression.
https://github.com/azahar-emu/azahar/pull/2318

The optional Old3DS syscore diagnostic policy is original Cara code; its interface
references are listed in old3ds_syscore_policy.h. It is not a port of external code
and remains OFF by default with hardware edge behavior unverified.

Optional Mac CPU JIT: Dynarmic (MerryMage and contributors), revision
b3a92ab54dadd26a0c2a87d2677b80249d2e1a5a, with retained local fmt6, ARM64 ABI/tick
and MAP_FAILED compatibility repairs. See emulator/externals/dynarmic/LICENSE.txt
and bundled dependency licenses there, plus docs/evidence/m1-dynarmic-source-manifest.json.
The original CPU adapter attribution is retained in emulator/src/core/arm/dynarmic.

